Rule 1 (broadcast compatibility of tensor shapes for element-wise divmod)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 2 (dividend tensor must have a non-complex numeric dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 3 (divisor tensor must have a non-complex numeric dtype)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 4 (divisor scalar must not be zero to prevent division by zero)
{v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= v_2 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 5 (boolean divisor must be true to avoid division by zero)
{v_2 : bool} |= v_2 = true
